-- title:
--   Squared geometric Frobenius fixes supersingular places over k̄
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field, $N$ a positive integer, and $q$ a prime with $\mathrm{char}\,k = q$ and $q \nmid N$. Let `data` be a `ModularPolynomialData q`, that is a monic $\Phi \in \mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ of degree $\psi(q)$ in $Y$ annihilating the pair consisting of the $q$-expansion substitution of the modular invariant, and let `hKr` assert the Kronecker congruence for it: the reduction of $\Phi$ coefficientwise modulo $q$ equals $(C(X)^q - X)\,(C(X) - X^q)$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/q)[X][Y]$. Consider the field $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldC k N`, the intermediate field of the Laurent series field over $k$ generated by the $q$-series $j$ and its $N$-fold substitution, and let $w$ be a place of $F$ over $k$, i.e. a valuation subring of $F$ containing $k$, different from $F$ and a principal ideal ring. Assume $w$ lies in `ssPlaces q N k`: $w$ is rational, is an affine geometric place, and the value of $w$ on the generator `jGeomGen k N` lies in the supersingular $j$-set `ssJSet q k`. Then applying `frobOnPlacesGeomLevel k N data hKr` twice to $w$ — each application restricting the place to the image of $F$ under $q$-power substitution on $q$-expansions and transporting it back along the induced isomorphism — returns $w$.
--
--   This records that the Frobenius correspondence acts as an involution on the supersingular points of the modular curve of level $N$ in characteristic $q$, the place-theoretic form of the statement that supersingular $j$-invariants in characteristic $q$ are defined over $\mathbb{F}_{q^2}$. It is used downstream in the analysis of reduction and specialisation of places on modular curves at supersingular points.
